## 2️⃣ Historic Barri Gòtic & La Rambla Loop  
**Ideal for:** First‑time tourists, history buffs, photographers, foodies.  
**Total time:** 5‑6 h (perfect for a half‑day).  

| # | Stop | How to get there | Suggested time | Opening hours (key sites) | Ticket price (USD) | What to see / do |
|---|------|------------------|----------------|---------------------------|--------------------|-------------------|
| 1 | **Plaça de Catalunya** (starting point) | Metro **L1/L3** → *Catalunya* | 10 min | – | – | Central hub, great for people‑watching. |
| 2 | **La Rambla** (walk south) | Stroll 5 min | 30‑45 min | – | – | Street performers, flower stalls, **Mercat de la Boqueria** – sample jamón, fresh juices, tapas. |
| 3 | **Gran Teatre del Liceu** | On La Rambla | 15 min | 10:00‑20:00 (varies) | – | Photo‑op; optional backstage tour (if booked). |
| 4 | **Barri Gòtic – Gothic Quarter** | Turn into Carrer del Bisbe | 2‑2.5 h | Cathedral 08:00‑19:30 (Apr‑Oct) / 08:30‑18:30 (Nov‑Mar) | Cathedral: $9 (adult) | • **Barcelona Cathedral** – climb rooftop for old‑city panorama. <br>• **Plaça del Rei** – medieval royal palace, Roman walls. <br>• **Plaça Sant Jaume** – city hall & Catalan government. <br>• **El Call** (Jewish Quarter) – narrow alleys, hidden courtyards. |
| 5 | **El Born** (adjacent) | Walk 5 min | 1‑1.5 h | Picasso Museum 10:00‑20:00 (Apr‑Oct) / 10:00‑19:00 (Nov‑Mar) – $16 (adult) | • **Santa Maria del Mar** – Gothic basilica. <br>• **Picasso Museum** – 2‑hour visit (reserve tickets). <br>• **Passeig del Born** – trendy cafés, artisan shops. |
